Notice the empty `catch (Exception e) { }` inside increment(). What is the risk?,"None - the finally still unlocks, so the code is safe","The lock is released correctly, but any failure inside the critical section vanishes without a trace. The caller sees a normal return and cannot tell that the increment did not happen",It causes the lock to be released twice,It converts the exception into an InterruptedException,,2,"Same silent-failure shape as the parking lot's release() printing instead of throwing, and the vending machine cancel() that announced a refund it never made. The lock handling is fine

