Actual output when this is run:

    t3 acquired lock in outer
    t4 trying to get lock in inner
    t4 ignored the lock
    t3 acquired lock in inner

t4 is refused immediately rather than waiting. Which line is responsible, and what would change with `lock.lock()` instead?,The 200 ms sleep in Main - with lock() it would wait 200 ms,"The bare `tryLock()` with no timeout, which gives up at once. With lock() t4 would wait for the full 10 seconds until t3 finished, then print 'acquired lock in inner' instead","The finally block, which rejects other threads",Nothing would change - lock() and tryLock() behave the same,,2,"Three different waiting behaviours in one class: lock() waits forever, tryLock() gives up instantly, tryLock(time, unit) waits a set period. Choosing between them is the whole point of explicit locks.",2

