Suppose wait() were replaced with Thread.sleep(). What would happen to this program?,"It would behave the same, just on a fixed timer","It would freeze. A sleeping thread keeps the lock, so the consumer would sit inside the synchronized method holding the lock while the producer waits outside to get in - neither can ever make progress",It would run faster because no notify is needed,The producer would throw IllegalMonitorStateException,,2,"Sleeping and waiting look similar and differ in the one way that matters here: sleep keeps the lock, wait gives it up.",2

