notify() is called at the end of both methods. What does it actually do?,Immediately hands control to the other thread,"Marks one waiting thread as ready to run again. That thread still has to reacquire the lock, so it only continues after the notifying thread leaves the synchronized method",Releases the lock straight away,Wakes every waiting thread,,2,"notify() is a signal, not a handover. The woken thread joins the queue for the lock like anyone else, which is why the notify can safely sit before the end of the method.",2

